        "description": "How to repair water-damaged drywall after storms and leaks in Central Florida homes.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/water-damage-drywall-repair-central-florida/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Water Damage Drywall Repair",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/water-damage-drywall-repair-central-florida"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Water Damage Drywall Repair</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">Water Damage Drywall Repair in Central Florida</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        Storm leaks, plumbing failures, and roof damage. When to patch vs. replace, how to check for mold.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            Water-damaged <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">drywall</a> is common in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, and Central Florida—summer storms, roof leaks, and plumbing failures all cause it. Here's when you can patch, when you need to cut and replace, and what to watch for in Florida's humidity.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Can You Patch Water-Damaged Drywall?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            It depends on how wet it got and how long it stayed wet.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Minor Water Damage (patch it)</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Ceiling or wall got damp but dried within 24-48 hours</li>
            <li>No visible mold or musty smell</li>
            <li>Paper surface is intact (no peeling or bubbling)</li>
            <li>Drywall feels solid when you push on it</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            These can usually be patched. Sand any raised edges, prime the stain with stain-blocking primer (Kilz or BIN), then <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">paint</a> to match. The primer is critical—water stains bleed through regular paint.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Moderate to Severe Damage (replace it)</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Drywall stayed wet longer than 48 hours</li>
            <li>Paper is peeling, bubbling, or falling off</li>
            <li>Drywall feels soft or spongy when you push on it</li>
            <li>You see mold spots (black, green, or fuzzy patches)</li>
            <li>There's a musty or moldy smell</li>
            <li>Ceiling is sagging or bowed</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            These need to be cut out and replaced. Patching over wet or moldy drywall just hides the problem until it gets worse. We cut out the damaged section, check studs and insulation for mold, replace with new drywall, texture to match, and paint.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Florida humidity rule:</strong> Central Florida's year-round humidity slows drying and speeds mold growth. If drywall got soaked, don't assume it's dry just because the surface feels okay—moisture can be trapped behind it. When in doubt, cut it out.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Common Causes of Water Damage in Central Florida</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Roof Leaks from Storms</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Summer storms and hurricanes cause shingle damage, flashing failures, and valley leaks. Water seeps into the attic and soaks ceiling drywall. Older homes with worn roofs get hit hardest.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Plumbing Failures</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Leaking pipes, failed toilet seals, and washing machine hoses soak walls and floors. Slow leaks behind walls go unnoticed for months—by the time you see a stain, there's usually mold behind it.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. AC Condensation & Duct Leaks</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Clogged AC drain pans overflow into ceilings. Poorly insulated ducts sweat condensation in attics, dripping onto drywall below. Common in older homes with attic HVAC systems.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Window & Door Leaks</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Wind-driven rain seeps around windows and doors with worn caulk or bad flashing. Water runs down inside the wall, soaking drywall at the bottom. You'll see peeling paint or dark stains along baseboards first.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How to Check for Mold</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Mold grows fast in Florida humidity—sometimes within 24-48 hours of water intrusion. Here's how to check:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Look for visible spots:</strong> Black, green, or white fuzzy patches on drywall, studs, or insulation</li>
            <li><strong>Smell for mustiness:</strong> Moldy drywall smells musty even if you can't see it yet</li>
            <li><strong>Check behind the damage:</strong> When we cut out water-damaged drywall, we inspect studs and insulation. Mold often hides behind the drywall surface.</li>
            <li><strong>Use a moisture meter:</strong> Pros use these to detect trapped moisture. Readings above 17% mean the drywall is still too wet and at risk for mold.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Small mold spots on drywall can be cleaned if caught early. Large patches or mold on studs usually mean you need professional remediation before we repair the drywall.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Repair Process</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Fix the Water Source</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Repairing drywall before fixing the leak is pointless—it'll just get wet again. Roof repairs, plumbing fixes, or caulking need to happen first. If you're not sure where water is coming from, we can help identify the source.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Dry the Area Completely</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Wet drywall needs to dry fully before repair. In Central Florida's humidity, that can take 3-7 days depending on how soaked it was. Fans, dehumidifiers, and AC help. We check with a moisture meter before cutting or patching.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Cut Out Damaged Sections</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We cut clean lines around water damage, removing soft or moldy drywall. Cuts go to the nearest stud for solid backing. If insulation behind the drywall is wet or moldy, we pull that too.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Replace & Texture Match</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            New drywall is cut to fit, screwed to studs, taped, and mudded smooth. We match existing texture (orange peel, knockdown, smooth, or <a href="/guides/popcorn-ceiling-removal-kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">popcorn</a>), prime, and paint. The patch should disappear.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How Much Does Water Damage Repair Cost?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Cost depends on the size of damage, mold presence, and ceiling vs. wall location:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Small patch (2x2 ft):</strong> $150-$300</li>
            <li><strong>Medium section (4x4 ft):</strong> $300-$600</li>
            <li><strong>Large ceiling repair (8x8 ft):</strong> $600-$1,200</li>
            <li><strong>Full room drywall replacement:</strong> $1,500-$3,500</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Mold remediation (if needed) adds $500-$3,000+ depending on extent. We work with mold specialists when the damage is severe. Insurance often covers water damage repairs if the leak was sudden (burst pipe, storm damage)—not if it was a slow leak you ignored.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">When to Call a Pro</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Small stains from a quick roof drip can be patched DIY if you catch them early. Call a pro when:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Drywall is soft, spongy, or sagging</li>
            <li>You see or smell mold</li>
            <li>Damage is on a ceiling (working overhead is awkward and dangerous)</li>
            <li>You don't know where the water is coming from</li>
            <li>The damage is larger than 2x2 feet</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We handle <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">drywall</a> repair across <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, <a href="/areas/st-cloud" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">St. Cloud</a>, and <a href="/areas/central-florida" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Central Florida</a>. Free estimates—we'll assess the damage, check for mold, and give you an itemized quote.
          </p>

          <div class="text-center mt-12">
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-6 font-sans">Water damage in your Central Florida home?</p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Fast, Clean Water Damage Drywall Repair"
    description="Cut out the damage, check for mold, patch it right. Serving Central Florida."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
